      <span class="hljs-bullet">-</span> <span class="hljs-string">MYSQL_PASSWORD=webgoat</span>
</code></div></div></pre><p>With this setup, the MySQL service is defined in a separate Dockerfile, and the Apache service is defined in the main Dockerfile. The docker-compose.yml file includes both services and sets up the necessary environment variables.</p><p>To build and run the containers, navigate to the root directory of the OWASPWebGoatPHP project and run:</p><pre><div class="bg-black rounded-md mb-4"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><span>bash</span><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"></svg>Copy code</div><div><code class="!whitespace-pre hljs language-bash">docker-compose up -d
