</code></div></div></pre><p>This docker-compose.yml file uses the official MySQL 5.7 image and configures the environment variables according to the Vagrant files. It also maps the MySQL port to the host.</p><p>With this setup, you can build and run the containers by navigating to the root directory of the OWASPWebGoatPHP project and running:</p><pre><div class="bg-black rounded-md mb-4"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><span>bash</span><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"></svg>Copy code</div><div><code class="!whitespace-pre hljs language-bash">docker-compose up -d
</code></div></div></pre><p>You can access WebGoatPHP at <a href="http://localhost:8080" target="_new">http://localhost:8080</a>.</p></div>'},  {'from': 'human', 'value': 'reduce container sizes by switching to alpine based images and provide updated Dockerfile and docker-compose.yml'},  {'from': 'gpt', 'value': '<div><p>To reduce container sizes, you can switch to Alpine-based images for both the web application and the database. Here's the updated Dockerfile and docker-compose.yml file using Alpine-based images:</p><p>Dockerfile:</p><pre><div class="bg-black rounded-md mb-4"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><span>Dockerfile</span><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"></svg>Copy code</div><div><code class="!whitespace-pre hljs language-Dockerfile">FROM php:7.4-apache-alpine

# Install necessary PHP extensions and enable Apache rewrite module
RUN docker-php-ext-install mysqli &amp;&amp; \
    apk add --no-cache apache2-utils &amp;&amp; \
    apk add --no-cache --virtual .build-deps $PHPIZE_DEPS &amp;&amp; \
    docker-php-ext-install gd &amp;&amp; \
    docker-php-ext-enable gd &amp;&amp; \
    apk del .build-deps &amp;&amp; \
    apk add --no-cache libpng libjpeg-turbo freetype &amp;&amp; \
    apk add --no-cache --upgrade grep &amp;&amp; \
    apk add --no-cache libxml2-dev &amp;&amp; \
    docker-php-ext-install soap &amp;&amp; \
    apk del libxml2-dev

RUN sed -i 's#AllowOverride None#AllowOverride All#' /etc/apache2/httpd.conf &amp;&amp; \
    sed -i 's#^DocumentRoot ".*#DocumentRoot "/var/www/html"#g' /etc/apache2/httpd.conf &amp;&amp; \
    sed -i 's#^&lt;Directory ".*#&lt;Directory "/var/www/html"&gt;#g' /etc/apache2/httpd.conf &amp;&amp; \
    printf "\n&lt;FilesMatch \.php$&gt;\n\tSetHandler application/x-httpd-php\n&lt;/FilesMatch&gt;\n" &gt;&gt; /etc/apache2/httpd.conf

# Copy the project files
COPY . /var/www/html/
RUN chown -R apache:apache /var/www/html/

EXPOSE 80
</code></div></div></pre><p>docker-compose.yml:</p><pre><div class="bg-black rounded-md mb-4"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><span>yaml</span><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"></svg>Copy code</div><div><code class="!whitespace-pre hljs language-yaml"><span class="hljs-attr">version:</span> <span class="hljs-string">'3.8'</span>

