</code></div></div></pre><p>This function takes in a <code>Server</code>, <code>PublicKeyCredentialCreationOptions</code>, and a <code>PublicKeyCredentialSourceRepository</code>. The <code>Server</code> is responsible for creating and checking the attestation, while the <code>PublicKeyCredentialCreationOptions</code> and <code>PublicKeyCredentialSourceRepository</code> are used for setting up the registration ceremony and managing the credential storage, respectively.</p><p>You'll need to implement the <code>isAttestationTrustworthy</code> function that checks the trustworthiness of the attestation based on your application's trust anchors and policy.</p></div>'},  {'from': 'human', 'value': '1 / 1continue'},  {'from': 'gpt', 'value': '<div><p>In order to proceed with the implementation, you'll need to set up the WebAuthn server, create the necessary PublicKeyCredentialCreationOptions, and implement the PublicKeyCredentialSourceRepository.</p><p>Here's an example of how to set up the WebAuthn server and create PublicKeyCredentialCreationOptions:</p><pre><div class="bg-black rounded-md mb-4"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><span>php</span><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"></svg>Copy code</div><div><code class="!whitespace-pre hljs language-php"><span class="hljs-meta">&lt;?php</span>

