</code></div></div></pre><p>To use this function, you will need to provide a WebAuthn server, PublicKeyCredentialCreationOptions, PublicKeyCredentialSourceRepository, trust anchors, and an AuthenticatorAttestationResponse from the client-side registration ceremony.</p><p>For example:</p><pre><div class="bg-black rounded-md mb-4"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><span>php</span><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"></svg>Copy code</div><div><code class="!whitespace-pre hljs language-php"><span class="hljs-variable">$rpEntity</span> = <span class="hljs-keyword">new</span> <span class="hljs-title class_">PublicKeyCredentialRpEntity</span>(<span class="hljs-string">"My RP"</span>, <span class="hljs-string">"my-rp.example.com"</span>);
