  };

  <span class="hljs-comment">// Send the attestationResponse to your server-side PHP script using your preferred method (e.g., XMLHttpRequest, fetch, etc.)</span>
}
</code></div></div></pre><p>In your server-side PHP script, you will need to receive the <code>AuthenticatorAttestationResponse</code> sent by the client-side code, and use it with the <code>performRegistrationCeremony</code> function:</p><pre><div class="bg-black rounded-md mb-4"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><span>php</span><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"></svg>Copy code</div><div><code class="!whitespace-pre hljs language-php"><span class="hljs-comment">// Get the AuthenticatorAttestationResponse from the client-side registration ceremony</span>
