<span class="hljs-variable">$credentialSource</span> = <span class="hljs-title function_ invoke__">performRegistrationCeremony</span>(<span class="hljs-variable">$webAuthnServer</span>, <span class="hljs-variable">$creationOptions</span>, <span class="hljs-variable">$credentialSourceRepository</span>, <span class="hljs-variable">$trustAnchors</span>, <span class="hljs-variable">$response</span>);

<span class="hljs-comment">// The credentialSource now contains the registered credential.</span>
</code></div></div></pre><p>With this setup, you can handle the registration ceremony for the WebAuthn system both on the client-side and the server-side. Remember to configure the trust anchors, server settings, and other parameters based on your application's requirements and security policies.</p></div>'}]

