on request by canceling and rejecting it.</p></div>'},  {'from': 'human', 'value': 'but when we run the code, the authentication does not wait for bsa to complete the authentication, it will straight away continue to success'},  {'from': 'gpt', 'value': '<div class="markdown prose w-full break-words dark:prose-invert dark"><p>It looks like the problem is that the "bsa" block of code is not being executed in the current configuration. This block is used to perform additional authentication checks, such as MFA, before the request is accepted or rejected.</p><p>It seems that the "bsa" block is inside the if(ok) condition, which checks if the authentication request is successful. Since the request is successful before the bsa block is executed, the bsa block will not be executed.</p><p>You might want to move the "bsa" block out of the if(ok) condition, and place it before the condition, so the bsa block will be executed before the request is determined as successful.</p><p>Additionally, you may want to check the logs of the RADIUS server for more information, and verify that the "bsa" block is being executed as expected.</p><p>It's recommended to test your configuration and fine-tune it before deploying it to a production environment, and also to consult the official documentation of the RADIUS server, which will provide more detailed instructions on how to configure and troubleshoot the server.</p></div>'},  {'from': 'human', 'value': 'but what do we need to add in the code to let radius wait for bsa authentication before proceed to allow or denied the authentication'},  {'from': 'gpt', 'value': '<div class="markdown prose w-full break-words dark:prose-invert dark"><p>In order to make FreeRADIUS wait for the "bsa" block to complete before proceeding with the authentication, you will need to add a return statement within the "bsa" block. The return statement will tell FreeRADIUS to wait for the completion of the "bsa" block before moving on to the next step of the authentication process.</p><p>Here is an example of how the code could look like:</p><pre><div class="bg-black mb-4 rounded-md"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><button class="flex ml-auto gap-2"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M16 4h2a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v14a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H6a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V6a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h2"></path><rect x="8" y="2" width="8" height="4" rx="1" ry="1"></rect></svg>Copy code</button></div><div class="p-4 overflow-y-auto"><code class="!whitespace-pre-wrap hljs language-go">ldap

