</code></div></div></pre></div>'},  {'from': 'human', 'value': 'how about the code in /etc/freeradius/3.0/sites-enabled/default? do i still need it?'},  {'from': 'gpt', 'value': '<div class="markdown prose w-full break-words dark:prose-invert dark"><p>The code in the "default" file located in "/etc/freeradius/3.0/sites-enabled" is the default configuration for the FreeRADIUS server. This code is executed when a client tries to connect to the server and no specific virtual server is defined for the client.</p><p>You don't need to remove the default file, but you will need to include your new virtual server, "my_virtual_server" in the default file so that the server knows to use it for authentication.</p><p>You can include your new virtual server by adding the following line at the end of the default file:</p><pre><div class="bg-black mb-4 rounded-md"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><button class="flex ml-auto gap-2"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M16 4h2a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v14a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H6a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V6a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h2"></path><rect x="8" y="2" width="8" height="4" rx="1" ry="1"></rect></svg>Copy code</button></div><div class="p-4 overflow-y-auto"><code class="!whitespace-pre-wrap hljs language-bash"><span class="hljs-variable">$INCLUDE</span> sites-enabled/my_virtual_server
</code></div></div></pre><p>This will tell the server to include the configurations in your new virtual server file when it's processing the requests.</p><p>It's recommended to check the official documentation of FreeRADIUS to find out how to include virtual servers.</p></div>'},  {'from': 'human', 'value': 'which part do i need to add the $INCLUDE sites-enabled/my_virtual_server'},  {'from': 'gpt', 'value': '<div class="markdown prose w-full break-words dark:prose-invert dark"><p>You need to add the <code>$INCLUDE sites-enabled/my_virtual_server</code> line in the "default" file located in the "/etc/freeradius/3.0/sites-enabled" directory.</p><p>This file is the main configuration file for the FreeRADIUS server. You can find the following section in the file:</p><pre><div class="bg-black mb-4 rounded-md"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><button class="flex ml-auto gap-2"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M16 4h2a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v14a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H6a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V6a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h2"></path><rect x="8" y="2" width="8" height="4" rx="1" ry="1"></rect></svg>Copy code</button></div><div class="p-4 overflow-y-auto"><code class="!whitespace-pre-wrap hljs language-javascript">server <span class="hljs-keyword">default</span> {
