ownload and install Wireshark: Visit the official Wireshark website (<a href="https://www.wireshark.org" target="_new">https://www.wireshark.org</a>) to download and install the appropriate version for your operating system.</p></li><li><p>Launch Wireshark: Open the Wireshark application on your computer.</p></li><li><p>Choose the network interface: In the main Wireshark window, you'll see a list of network interfaces. Select the one that corresponds to the network traffic you want to observe (e.g., Wi-Fi, Ethernet).</p></li><li><p>Start capturing packets: Click the "Start" button (shark fin icon) to begin capturing packets on the selected interface.</p></li><li><p>Apply an HTTP filter: To focus on HTTP traffic, type "http" (without quotes) in the filter bar and press Enter. This will show only packets related to the HTTP protocol.</p></li><li><p>Inspect packets: Click on individual packets to view detailed information, such as source and destination IP addresses, HTTP headers, and any transmitted data in plain text.</p></li><li><p>Stop capturing: When you've captured enough data or want to stop monitoring, click the "Stop" button (square icon) in the Wireshark toolbar.</p></li></ol><p>Remember to respect the privacy of others and only capture traffic for which you have proper authorization or that is generated by your own devices and applications.</p></div>'}]

[ {'from': 'human', 'value': 'CVE description: 
A flaw was found in the way the "flags" member of the new pipe buffer structure was lacking proper initialization in copy_page_to_iter_pipe and push_pipe functions in the Linux kernel and could thus contain stale values. An unprivileged local user could use this flaw to write to pages in the page cache backed by read only files and as such escalate their privileges on the system.

   :
static size_t copy_page_to_iter_pipe(struct page *page, size_t offset, size_t bytes,
       struct iov_iter *i)
{
  struct pipe_inode_info *pipe = i-&gt;pipe;
  struct pipe_buffer *buf;
  unsigned int p_tail = pipe-&gt;tail;
  unsigned int p_mask = pipe-&gt;ring_size - 1;
  unsigned int i_head = i-&gt;head;
  size_t off;

  if (unlikely(bytes &gt; i-&gt;count))
    bytes = i-&gt;count;

  if (unlikely(!bytes))
    return 0;

  if (!sanity(i))
    return 0;

  off = i-&gt;iov_offset;
  buf = &amp;pipe-&gt;bufs[i_head &amp; p_mask];
  if (off) {
    if (offset == off &amp;&amp; buf-&gt;page == page) {
      /* merge with the last one */
      buf-&gt;len += bytes;
      i-&gt;iov_offset += bytes;
      goto out;
    }
    i_head++;
    buf = &amp;pipe-&gt;bufs[i_head &amp; p_mask];
  }
  if (pipe_full(i_head, p_tail, pipe-&gt;max_usage))
    return 0;

  buf-&gt;ops = &amp;page_cache_pipe_buf_ops;
  get_page(page);
  buf-&gt;page = page;
  buf-&gt;offset = offset;
  buf-&gt;len = bytes;

  pipe-&gt;head = i_head + 1;
  i-&gt;iov_offset = offset + bytes;
  i-&gt;head = i_head;
out:
  i-&gt;count -= bytes;
  return bytes;
}

          '},  {'from': 'gpt', 'value': '<div><p>  "flags"       .   pipe buffer  , copy_page_to_iter_pipe()   .</p><p>     , pipe buffer "flags"      push_pipe()      . push_pipe()   pipe buffer  "flags"   buffer   ,  buffer   .  ,  buffer        ,          .</p><p>  , push_pipe()   pipe buffer   "flags"       .  , pipe buffer   , flags  0  .    buffer    ,          .</p></div>'},  {'from': 'human', 'value': '     '},  {'from': 'gpt', 'value': '<div><p>   , push_pipe()   pipe buffer   "flags"    .        :</p><pre><div class="bg-black rounded-md mb-4"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><span>c</span><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"></svg>Copy code</div><div><code class="!whitespace-pre hljs language-c">new_buf = alloc_pipe_info(pipe);
<span class="hljs-keyword">if</span> (!new_buf)
    <span class="hljs-keyword">goto</span> fail;

new_buf-&gt;flags = <span class="hljs-number">0</span>; <span class="hljs-comment">// flags   0 </span>

<span class="hljs-comment">/* Copy data from old buffer to new buffer */</span>
<span class="hljs-built_in">memcpy</span>(new_buf-&gt;page, buf-&gt;page, PAGE_SIZE);
new_buf-&gt;len = buf-&gt;len;
new_buf-&gt;offset = buf-&gt;offset;

pipe-&gt;bufs[i &amp; mask] = new_buf;
</code></div></div></pre><p>   buffer  ,  buffer flags   0 ,  buffer   buffer .  ,  buffer    buffer         ,  buffer      buffer    .</p><p>    push_pipe()        .</p></div>'}]

[ {'from': 'human', 'value': 'hello karim, I need to setup a multifactor authentication for my mikrotik vpn. here is the requirement.

1. Radius
