<code>ln -s /etc/freeradius/3.0/mods-available/bsa /etc/freeradius/3.0/mods-enabled/bsa</code></p><p>Make sure the bsa module is enabled in the radiusd.conf file, the file is located in the /etc/freeradius/3.0 folder.</p><p>You may also need to restart the FreeRADIUS service after making these changes.</p><p>It's recommended to check the official documentation of FreeRADIUS to find out how to enable and configure modules.</p><p>Also, you can use the <code>radiusd -X</code> command to start the server in debug mode, this will allow you to see the logs of the server and find out what is causing the error.</p></div>'},  {'from': 'human', 'value': 'yes, i know that and its already enable but there's and error if I add "if" statement in the module. here is the error.. /etc/freeradius/3.0/mods-enabled/bsa[9]: Invalid location for 'if''},  {'from': 'gpt', 'value': '<div class="markdown prose w-full break-words dark:prose-invert dark"><p>I apologize for the confusion, it seems that the "if" statement is not allowed in the module configuration file, as it is not a valid location for the statement.</p><p>It's recommended to move the "if" statement outside of the module in a virtual server file located in the "/etc/freeradius/3.0/sites-enabled" directory.</p><p>You can create a new file for example "my_virtual_server" and add the following configuration:</p><pre><div class="bg-black mb-4 rounded-md"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><button class="flex ml-auto gap-2"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M16 4h2a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v14a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H6a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V6a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h2"></path><rect x="8" y="2" width="8" height="4" rx="1" ry="1"></rect></svg>Copy code</button></div><div class="p-4 overflow-y-auto"><code class="!whitespace-pre-wrap hljs language