ls the <code>Run</code> method of the <code>IWshShell3</code> object to execute a command in a new command prompt window. The command being executed is <code>gpresult /scope:computer /v 1&gt; config\gpresult.txt 2&gt;&amp;1</code>, which generates a Group Policy Results report for the computer and writes it to a file named "gpresult.txt" in the "config" folder. The <code>0</code> parameter passed to the <code>Run</code> method indicates that the command prompt window should be hidden, and the <code>"false"</code> parameter indicates that the script should not wait for the command to complete before continuing.</p></li></ol><p>In summary, this code expands two environment variables to their full paths, checks whether a folder named "config" exists, and then runs a command that generates a Group Policy Results report for the computer and writes it to a file named "gpresult.txt" in the "config" folder.</p></div>'}]

