[ {'from': 'human', 'value': 'write to me secure query in MSSQL'},  {'from': 'gpt', 'value': '<div><p>To write a secure query in MSSQL, you should follow these best practices:</p><ol><li>Use parameterized queries: Instead of concatenating user input into your SQL query, use parameterized queries to prevent SQL injection attacks.</li></ol><p>Example:</p><pre><div class="bg-black rounded-md mb-4"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><span>sql</span><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"></svg>Copy code</div><div><code class="!whitespace-pre hljs language-sql"><span class="hljs-keyword">DECLARE</span> <span class="hljs-variable">@Username</span> <span class="hljs-type">VARCHAR</span>(<span class="hljs-number">50</span>) <span class="hljs-operator">=</span> <span class="hljs-string">'John'</span>;
<span class="hljs-keyword">DECLARE</span> <span class="hljs-variable">@Password</span> <span class="hljs-type">VARCHAR</span>(<span class="hljs-number">50</span>) <span class="hljs-operator">=</span> <span class="hljs-string">'password123'</span>;

<span class="hljs-keyword">SELECT</span> <span class="hljs-operator">*</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">FROM</span> Users
<span class="hljs-keyword">WHERE</span> Username <span class="hljs-operator">=</span> <span class="hljs-variable">@Username</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">AND</span> Password <span class="hljs-operator">=</span> <span class="hljs-variable">@Password</span>;
</code></div></div></pre><ol><li><p>Limit permissions: Give the least privilege necessary to users and applications. Avoid using elevated privileges for normal operations.</p></li><li><p>Use strong authentication: Use strong authentication methods like Windows authentication or SQL authentication with strong passwords to protect against unauthorized access.</p></li><li><p>Encrypt sensitive data: Use Transparent Data Encryption (TDE) or Always Encrypted to protect sensitive data at rest.</p></li></ol><p>Example:</p><pre><div class="bg-black rounded-md mb-4"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><span>vbnet</span><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"></svg>Copy code</div><div><code class="!whitespace-pre hljs language-vbnet"><span class="hljs-keyword">SELECT</span> CreditCardNumber <span class="hljs-keyword">FROM</span> Customers
<span class="hljs-keyword">WHERE</span> Id = <span class="hljs-number">123</span>
<span class="hljs-keyword">FOR</span> JSON <span class="hljs-keyword">AUTO</span>, ENCRYPTED <span class="hljs-keyword">WITH</span> (<span class="hljs-keyword">KEY</span> = <span class="hljs-comment">'MyEncryptionKey');</span>
</code></div></div></pre><ol><li><p>Regularly update and patch MSSQL: Keep your MSSQL server up to date with the latest patches and security updates to protect against known vulnerabilities.</p></li><li><p>Monitor and audit database activity: Set up logging and auditing to detect any unusual or suspicious database activity.</p></li></ol><p>Example:</p><pre><div class="bg-black rounded-md mb-4"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><span>sql</span><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"></svg>Copy code</div><div><code class="!whitespace-pre hljs language-sql"><span class="hljs-keyword">CREATE</span> SERVER AUDIT MyAudit
<span class="hljs-keyword">TO</span> FILE (FILEPATH <span class="hljs-operator">=</span> <span class="hljs-string">'C:\AuditLogs\'</span>, MAXSIZE <span class="hljs-operator">=</span> <span class="hljs-number">1</span> GB, MAX_FILES <span class="hljs-operator">=</span> <span class="hljs-number">100</span>)
<span class="hljs-keyword">WITH</span> (ON_FAILURE <span class="hljs-operator">=</span> CONTINUE_AUDIT_AFTER_FAILURE);

