</code></div></div></pre><p>By following these best practices, you can write secure queries in MSSQL and protect your data from unauthorized access or attack.</p></div>'},  {'from': 'human', 'value': 'continue'},  {'from': 'gpt', 'value': '<div><ol><li>Use appropriate data types: Use appropriate data types for your database columns and variables to prevent unexpected data conversions or truncation, which can lead to security vulnerabilities.</li></ol><p>Example:</p><pre><div class="bg-black rounded-md mb-4"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><span>sql</span><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"></svg>Copy code</div><div><code class="!whitespace-pre hljs language-sql"><span class="hljs-keyword">CREATE</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">TABLE</span> Employees
