show me how to using this mssql"},  {'from': 'gpt', 'value': '<div><p>Sure, here's an example of how to use the <code>mssql</code> package in Node.js to connect to a SQL Server database and run a simple query:</p><pre><div class="bg-black rounded-md mb-4"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><span>javascript</span><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"></svg>Copy code</div><div><code class="!whitespace-pre hljs language-javascript"><span class="hljs-keyword">const</span> sql = <span class="hljs-built_in">require</span>(<span class="hljs-string">'mssql'</span>);

<span class="hljs-comment">// Define the configuration for the SQL Server connection</span>
<span class="hljs-keyword">const</span> config = {
  <span class="hljs-attr">server</span>: <span class="hljs-string">'localhost'</span>,
  <span class="hljs-attr">database</span>: <span class="hljs-string">'MyDatabase'</span>,
  <span class="hljs-attr">user</span>: <span class="hljs-string">'MyUsername'</span>,
