explain to me'},  {'from': 'gpt', 'value': '<div><p><code>request.input</code> is a method in the <code>mssql</code> package for creating and adding input parameters to a SQL query. Input parameters can be used to pass values to a SQL query without directly concatenating them into the query string, which helps to prevent SQL injection attacks and also make the code more readable.</p><p>Here's an example of how to use <code>request.input()</code>:</p><pre><div class="bg-black rounded-md mb-4"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><span>javascript</span><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"></svg>Copy code</div><div><code class="!whitespace-pre hljs language-javascript"><span class="hljs-keyword">const</span> sql = <span class="hljs-built_in">require</span>(<span class="hljs-string">'mssql'</span>);

<span class="hljs-keyword">async</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">function</span> <span class="hljs-title function_">executeQuery</span>(<span class="hljs-params"></span>) {
  <span class="hljs-keyword">try</span> {
    <span class="hljs-comment">// Create a new SQL Server connection pool</span>
    <span class="hljs-keyword">const</span> pool = <span class="hljs-keyword">await</span> sql.<span class="hljs-title function_">connect</span>(config);

    <span class="hljs-comment">// Create a new SQL request object</span>
    <span class="hljs-keyword">const</span> request = <span class="hljs-keyword">new</span> sql.<span class="hljs-title class_">Request</span>(pool);

    <span class="hljs-comment">// Add input parameters to the request</span>
    request.<span class="hljs-title function_">input</span>(<span class="hljs-string">'username'</span>, sql.<span class="hljs-title class_">NVarChar</span>(<span class="hljs-number">50</span>), <span class="hljs-string">'john'</span>);
    request.<span class="hljs-title function_">input</span>(<span class="hljs-string">'password'</span>, sql.<span class="hljs-title class_">NVarChar</span>(<span class="hljs-number">50</span>), <span class="hljs-string">'password123'</span>);

    <span class="hljs-comment">// Execute a SQL query using the input parameters</span>
    <span class="hljs-keyword">const</span> result = <span class="hljs-keyword">await</span> request.<span class="hljs-title function_">query</span>(<span class="hljs-string">`SELECT * FROM Users WHERE Username = @username AND Password = @password`</span>);

    <span class="hljs-variable language_">console</span>.<span class="hljs-title function_">log</span>(result.<span class="hljs-property">recordset</span>);

  } <span class="hljs-keyword">catch</span> (err) {
    <span class="hljs-variable language_">console</span>.<span class="hljs-title function_">error</span>(<span class="hljs-string">'Error executing SQL query:'</span>, err.<span class="hljs-property">message</span>);
  }
}
</code></div></div></pre><p>In this example, we first create a new SQL Server connection pool using the <code>sql.connect()</code> method. We then create a new <code>sql.Request</code> object and use the <code>request.input()</code> method to add two input parameters, <code>username</code> and <code>password</code>, with corresponding data types of <code>sql.NVarChar(50)</code> (a Unicode string with a maximum length of 50 characters).</p><p>Finally, we execute a SQL query that uses these input parameters in</p></div>'}]

