    [<span class="hljs-meta">Required</span>]
    <span class="hljs-keyword">public</span> DateTimeOffset CreatedOn { <span class="hljs-keyword">get</span>; <span class="hljs-keyword">set</span>; }

    <span class="hljs-keyword">public</span> DateTimeOffset? ModifiedOn { <span class="hljs-keyword">get</span>; <span class="hljs-keyword">set</span>; }
}
</code></div></div></pre><p>In this example, the <code>OAuthCredentials</code> class represents a table in your database that will store the information needed to obtain access tokens using MSAL.NET. The table has the following columns:</p><ul><li><code>Id</code>: An integer ID that uniquely identifies each row in the table. This column is marked with the <code>[Key]</code> attribute to indicate that it is the primary key.</li><li><code>ClientId</code>: A string that represents the client ID of the application that will be using the access token.</li><li><code>ClientSecret</code>: A string that represents the client secret of the application that will be using the access token. This column should be encrypted or otherwise protected to prevent unauthorized access.</li><li><code>TenantId</code>: A string that represents the ID of the Azure AD tenant that the application belongs to.</li><li><code>Authority</code>: A string that represents the authority URL of the Azure AD instance that the application will be authenticating against.</li><li><code>RedirectUri</code>: An optional string that represents the URI that the user will be redirected to after authentication.</li><li><code>Scopes</code>: An optional string that represents the permissions that the application will be requesting.</li><li><code>Username</code>: An optional string that represents the username of the user that will be authenticated with ROPC flow.</li><li><code>Password</code>: An optional string that represents the password of the user that will be authenticated with ROPC flow. This column should be encrypted or otherwise protected to prevent unauthorized access.</li><li><code>CreatedOn</code>: A DateTimeOffset that represents the date and time that the row was created.</li><li><code>ModifiedOn</code>: An optional DateTimeOffset that represents the date and time that the row was last modified.</li></ul><p>You can use Entity Framework Code First to create this table in your database by defining a DbContext that includes a DbSet property for your <code>OAuthCredentials</code> class, and then running the migration commands to create the database schema.</p></div>'},  {'from': 'human', 'value': "I'd likely also like a field to indicate what type of flow this record represents. And a field to store a refreshtoken, so I can use that in many cases to refresh the token."},  {'from': 'gpt', 'value': '<div class="markdown prose w-full break-words dark:prose-invert light"><p>Sure, here's an updated version of the <code>OAuthCredentials</code> class that includes a <code>FlowType</code> property to indicate the OAuth flow type, and a <code>RefreshToken</code> property to store the refresh token:</p><pre><div class="bg-black mb-4 rounded-md"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><span class="">csharp</span><button class="flex ml-auto gap-2"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M16 4h2a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v14a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H6a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V6a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h2"></path><rect x="8" y="2" width="8" height="4" rx="1" ry="1"></rect></svg>Copy code</button></div><div class="p-4 overflow-y-auto"><code class="!whitespace-pre hljs language-csharp"><span class="hljs-keyword">public</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">class</span> <span class="hljs-title">OAuthCredentials</span>
