        deadline = _deadline;
    }

    <span class="hljs-function">function <span class="hljs-title">deposit</span>() external payable</span> {
        require(now &lt; deadline);
        balance += msg.<span class="hljs-keyword">value</span>;
    }

    <span class="hljs-function">function <span class="hljs-title">withdraw</span>() external</span> {
        require(now &gt; deadline);
        msg.sender.transfer(balance);
    }
}
</code></div></div></pre><p>In this example, the <code>Victim</code> contract has a <code>setDeadline()</code> function that sets a deadline for when ether can be deposited into the contract, and a <code>withdraw()</code> function that allows ether to be withdrawn from the contract after the deadline has passed. However, the <code>now</code> keyword in solidity returns the current block's timestamp, which can be manipulated by the miner and it can lead to the attacker being able to deposit or withdraw ether before or after the deadline.</p><p>To prevent this type of vulnerability, it's recommended to use timestamps from a reliable oracle service, or to use a different source of randomness. An oracle service is a smart contract that provides external data, such as the current time, to other contracts on the blockchain. By using an oracle service, contracts can access external data that is resistant to manipulation by a miner. Another way is to use a block's timestamp, which is guaranteed to be unique and can be used to generate randomness.</p><p>Here's an example of how the same contract can be modified to prevent the vulnerability:</p><pre><div class="bg-black mb-4 rounded-md" bis_skin_checked="1"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans" bis_skin_checked="1"><button class="flex ml-auto gap-2"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M16 4h2a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v14a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H6a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V6a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h2"></path><rect x="8" y="2" width="8" height="4" rx="1" ry="1"></rect></svg>Copy code</button></div><div class="p-4 overflow-y-auto" bis_skin_checked="1"><code class="!whitespace-pre-wrap hljs">contract
