</code></div></div></pre><p>In this example, the <code>Victim</code> contract has a <code>register()</code> function that allows an address to be marked as "allowed" and a <code>doSomething()</code> function that can only be called by an "allowed" address. However, an attacker could create a large number of contracts with malicious code that call the <code>register()</code> function repeatedly, consuming all the gas of each block. This would prevent legitimate calls to the <code>doSomething()</code> function from being processed and cause a DoS attack.</p><p>To prevent this type of vulnerability, it's recommended to use a mechanism that limits the number of calls that can be made to a function in a given period of time, or to use a mechanism that limits the amount of gas that can be consumed by a contract during a given period of time. Another approach is to have a whitelist of addresses that are allowed to call the function, and only allow the function to be called by those addresses.</p><p>Here's an example of how the same contract can be modified to prevent the vulnerability:</p><pre><div class="bg-black mb-4 rounded-md" bis_skin_checked="1"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans" bis_skin_checked="1"><button class="flex ml-auto gap-2"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M16 4h2a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v14a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H6a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V6a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h2"></path><rect x="8" y="2" width="8" height="4" rx="1" ry="1"></rect></svg>Copy code</button></div><div class="p-4 overflow-y-auto" bis_skin_checked="1"><code class="!whitespace-pre-wrap hljs language-typescript">contract <span class="hljs-title class_">Victim</span> {
