    }

    function <span class="hljs-built_in">sell</span>(uint _value) public {
        <span class="hljs-built_in">require</span>(buyOrders[msg.sender] &gt;= _value);
        buyOrders<span class="hljs-selector-attr">[msg.sender]</span> -= _value;
        sellOrders<span class="hljs-selector-attr">[msg.sender]</span> += _value;
    }
}
</code></div></div></pre><p>In this example, the <code>Exchange</code> contract has a <code>buy()</code> function that allows users to place a buy order by sending ether to the contract, and a <code>sell()</code> function that allows users to sell their ether by specifying the amount they want to sell. However, an attacker could place a buy order for the same amount as another user's sell order, and execute the buy before the other user's sell order, effectively frontrunning the other user's transaction. This can allow the attacker to buy ether at a lower price than the market value.</p><p>To prevent this type of vulnerability, it's recommended to use a mechanism that ensures that transactions are executed in a predictable order, such as using a priority queue to order transactions by the time they are received, or using a random number generator to randomly order transactions. Another approach is to use a mechanism to ensure that the contract's state is not visible to external actors, such as using a zero-knowledge proof to hide the contract's state.</p><p>Here's an example of how the same contract can be modified to prevent the vulnerability:</p><pre><div class="bg-black mb-4 rounded-md" bis_skin_checked="1"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans" bis_skin_checked="1"><button class="flex ml-auto gap-2"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M16 4h2a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v14a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H6a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V6a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h2"></path><rect x="8" y="2" width="8" height="4" rx="1" ry="1"></rect></svg>Copy code</button></div><div class="p-4 overflow-y-auto" bis_skin_checked="1"><code class="!whitespace-pre-wrap hljs language-css">contract Exchange {
