[ {'from': 'human', 'value': 'Describe via code how to disable WebRTC encryption for capturing the RPT packets and using elsewhere, no websocket, no browser plugins and maybe using `setSctpSendEncryptStatus` or other approach?'},  {'from': 'gpt', 'value': '<div><p>WebRTC (Web Real-Time Communication) is a technology that enables real-time communication between web browsers and devices, including video and audio streaming, file transfer, and screen sharing. WebRTC uses end-to-end encryption to ensure the privacy and security of communication. Disabling WebRTC encryption is generally not recommended as it weakens the security of the communication and may expose sensitive data to interception.</p><p>However, if you still want to disable WebRTC encryption for the purpose of capturing RTP packets, you can use the following approach:</p><ol><li>Create a WebRTC peer connection using the <code>RTCPeerConnection</code> constructor.</li></ol><pre><div><div>Copy code</div><div><code><span>const</span> peerConnection = <span>new</span> <span>RTCPeerConnection</span>();
</code></div></div></pre><ol><li>Set the <code>sctpSendEncryptStatus</code> property of the peer connection to <code>false</code> using the <code>setSctpSendEncryptStatus</code> method. This will disable SCTP (Stream Control Transmission Protocol) encryption for data channels, which are used for peer-to-peer communication in WebRTC.</li></ol><pre><div><div>Copy code</div><div><code>peerConnection.<span>setSctpSendEncryptStatus</span>(<span>false</span>);
</code></div></div></pre><ol><li>Create an RTP sender using the <code>createSender</code> method of the peer connection and pass in the <code>audio</code> or <code>video</code> track as an argument. This will create an RTP sender that can be used to send audio or video data over the peer connection.</li></ol><pre><div><div>Copy code</div><div><code><span>const</span> audioTrack = <span>new</span> <span>MediaStreamTrack</span>();
<span>const</span> audioSender = peerConnection.<span>createSender</span>(audioTrack);
