</code></div></div></pre><p>To use CloudKit in your app, you will need to set up a CloudKit container in the Apple Developer portal and enable CloudKit in your Xcode project. Once you have set up CloudKit, you can use the <code>CloudKitService</code> class to interact with your CloudKit database.</p><p>Here is an example of how you could implement the <code>CloudKitService</code> class:</p><pre><div class="bg-black rounded-md mb-4"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><span>swift</span><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"></svg>Copy code</div><div><code class="!whitespace-pre hljs language-swift"><span class="hljs-keyword">import</span> CloudKit

<span class="hljs-keyword">class</span> <span class="hljs-title class_">CloudKitService</span> {
