}
</code></div></div></pre><p>In your <code>NetworkManager</code> class, you can use the <code>CloudKitService</code> to fetch and save users to CloudKit:</p><pre><div class="bg-black rounded-md mb-4"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><span>swift</span><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"></svg>Copy code</div><div><code class="!whitespace-pre hljs language-swift"><span class="hljs-keyword">class</span> <span class="hljs-title class_">NetworkManager</span>: <span class="hljs-title class_">ObservableObject</span> {
