Using the previous example, change the font for mnsLondonRegular
"},  {'from': 'gpt', 'value': '<div class="markdown prose w-full break-words dark:prose-invert light"><p>You can use the JSON object to set the custom font on a <code>div</code> element using styled-components. Here is an example of how you can do this:</p><pre><div class="bg-black mb-4 rounded-md"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><button class="flex ml-auto gap-2"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M16 4h2a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v14a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H6a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V6a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h2"></path><rect x="8" y="2" width="8" height="4" rx="1" ry="1"></rect></svg>Copy code</button></div><div class="p-4 overflow-y-auto"><code class="!whitespace-pre-wrap hljs language-javascript"><span class="hljs-keyword">import</span> styled <span class="hljs-keyword">from</span> <span class="hljs-string">'styled-components'</span>;

<span class="hljs-keyword">const</span> fontStyles = {
  <span class="hljs-attr">typography</span>: {
    <span class="hljs-attr">primary</span>: {
      <span class="hljs-attr">display</span>: <span class="hljs-string">'mnsLondonRegular'</span>,
      <span class="hljs-attr">semiBold</span>: <span class="hljs-string">'mnsLondonBold'</span>
    }
  }
}

<span class="hljs-keyword">const</span> <span class="hljs-title class_">CustomDiv</span> = styled.<span class="hljs-property">div</span><span class="hljs-string">`
  font-family: <span class="hljs-subst">${fontStyles.typography.primary.display}</span>, sans-serif;
`</span>;

<span class="hljs-keyword">function</span> <span class="hljs-title function_">MyComponent</span>(<span class="hljs-params"></span>) {
  <span class="hljs-keyword">return</span> <span class="xml"><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">CustomDiv</span>&gt;</span>This text has a custom font.<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">CustomDiv</span>&gt;</span></span>;
}
</code></div></div></pre><p>In this example, the <code>styled</code> function is used to create a styled component with the custom font <code>mnsLondonRegular</code>. This component is then used to render a <code>div</code> element with the custom font.</p><p>You will need to make sure that the custom font is imported or linked in your project, otherwise the custom font will not be applied.</p><p>Also, make sure that the font you want to use should be available in your project or should be imported or linked, otherwise the text will fallback to the default font.</p><p>And also, make sure that the path to the font you're trying to use is correct, as it is defined in the JSON object.</p><p>If you have the font files, you can import them in your project and then use them like any other font.</p><pre><div class="bg-black mb-4 rounded-md"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><button class="flex ml-auto gap-2"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M16 4h2a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v14a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H6a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V6a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h2"></path><rect x="8" y="2" width="8" height="4" rx="1" ry="1"></rect></svg>Copy code</button></div><div class="p-4 overflow-y-auto"><code class="!whitespace-pre-wrap hljs language-javascript"><span class="hljs-keyword">import</span> <span class="hljs-string">'./path/to/mnsLondonRegular.ttf'</span>
</code></div></div></pre><p>And then you can use the font family name that you imported as the font-family in your css</p><pre><div class="bg-black mb-4 rounded-md"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><button class="flex ml-auto gap-2"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M16 4h2a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v14a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H6a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V6a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h2"></path><rect x="8" y="2" width="8" height="4" rx="1" ry="1"></rect></svg>Copy code</button></div><div class="p-4 overflow-y-auto"><code class="!whitespace-pre-wrap hljs language-javascript"><span class="hljs-keyword">const</span> <span class="hljs-title class_">CustomDiv</span> = styled.<span class="hljs-property">div</span><span class="hljs-string">`
  font-family: 'mnsLondonRegular', sans-serif;
`</span>;
</code></div></div></pre><p>You can also use the <code>@font-face</code> CSS rule to import the font from a remote location.</p><pre><div class="bg-black mb-4 rounded-md"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><button class="flex ml-auto gap-2"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M16 4h2a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v14a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H6a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V6a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h2"></path><rect x="8" y="2" width="8" height="4" rx="1" ry="1"></rect></svg>Copy code</button></div><div class="p-4 overflow-y-auto"><code class="!whitespace-pre-wrap hljs language-CSS"><span class="hljs-keyword">@font-face</span> {
  <span class="hljs-attribute">font-family</span>: <span class="hljs-string">'mnsLondonRegular'</span>;
  <span class="hljs-attribute">src</span>: <span class="hljs-built_in">url</span>(<span class="hljs-string">'https://example.com/fonts/mnsLondonRegular.ttf'</span>);
}
</code></div></div></pre><p>Then you can use the font family name that you imported as the font-family in your css</p><pre><div class="bg-black mb-4 rounded-md"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><button class="flex ml-auto gap-2"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M16 4h2a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v14a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H6a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V6a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h2"></path><rect x="8" y="2" width="8" height="4" rx="1" ry="1"></rect></svg>Copy code</button></div><div class="p-4 overflow-y-auto"><code class="!whitespace-pre-wrap hljs language-javascript"><span class="hljs-keyword">const</span> <span class="hljs-title class_">CustomDiv</span> = styled.<span class="hljs-property">div</span><span class="hljs-string">`
  font-family: 'mnsLondonRegular', sans-serif;
`</span>;
</code></div></div></pre><p>Please note that some browsers may have issues with loading fonts from remote locations, and you may need to configure your server to serve the font files with the appropriate headers.</p></div>'},  {'from': 'human', 'value': 'How would that example look if mnsLondonRegular was possibly undefined?'},  {'from': 'gpt', 'value': '<div class="markdown prose w-full break-words dark:prose-invert light"><p>If the <code>mnsLondonRegular</code> property in the JSON object is possibly undefined, you can use a default value for the font family in case it is not defined. Here is an example of how you can do this using the <code>||</code> operator in javascript:</p><pre><div class="bg-black mb-4 rounded-md"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><button class="flex ml-auto gap-2"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M16 4h2a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v14a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H6a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V6a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h2"></path><rect x="8" y="2" width="8" height="4" rx="1" ry="1"></rect></svg>Copy code</button></div><div class="p-4 overflow-y-auto"><code class="!whitespace-pre-wrap hljs language-javascript"><span class="hljs-keyword">import</span> styled <span class="hljs-keyword">from</span> <span class="hljs-string">'styled-components'</span>;

<span class="hljs-keyword">const</span> fontStyles = {
  <span class="hljs-attr">typography</span>: {
    <span class="hljs-attr">primary</span>: {
      <span class="hljs-attr">semiBold</span>: <span class="hljs-string">'mnsLondonBold'</span>
    }
  }
}

<span class="hljs-keyword">const</span> <span class="hljs-title class_">CustomDiv</span> = styled.<span class="hljs-property">div</span><span class="hljs-string">`
  font-family: <span class="hljs-subst">${fontStyles.typography.primary.display || <span class="hljs-string">'sans-serif'</span>}</span>;
`</span>;

<span class="hljs-keyword">function</span> <span class="hljs-title function_">MyComponent</span>(<span class="hljs-params"></span>) {
  <span class="hljs-keyword">return</span> <span class="xml"><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">CustomDiv</span>&gt;</span>This text has a custom font.<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">CustomDiv</span>&gt;</span></span>;
}
</code></div></div></pre><p>In this example, if the <code>mnsLondonRegular</code> property is not defined, it will be treated as <code>undefined</code> when used in the template literal. The <code>||</code> operator will then evaluate <code>undefined</code> as <code>false</code> and return the value on the right side of the operator, in this case <code>'sans-serif'</code>. So, the <code>div</code> element will have the font-family 'sans-serif' as default in case the value of <code>mnsLondonRegular</code> is not defined or null.</p><p>You can also use the <code>?.</code> operator (optional chaining) if your project is using a version of javascript that supports it.</p><pre><div class="bg-black mb-4 rounded-md"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><button class="flex ml-auto gap-2"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M16 4h2a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v14a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H6a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V6a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h2"></path><rect x="8" y="2" width="8" height="4" rx="1" ry="1"></rect></svg>Copy code</button></div><div class="p-4 overflow-y-auto"><code class="!whitespace-pre-wrap hljs language-javascript"><span class="hljs-keyword">const</span> <span class="hljs-title class_">CustomDiv</span> = styled.<span class="hljs-property">div</span><span class="hljs-string">`
  font-family: <span class="hljs-subst">${fontStyles.typography?.primary?.display || <span class="hljs-string">'sans-serif'</span>}</span>;
`</span>;
</code></div></div></pre><p>This operator allows you to access the nested properties of an object without having to check for <code>null</code> or <code>undefined</code> values at each level.</p><p>Please note that this is a basic example, in a real-world scenario, you would probably want to handle the missing value in a more robust way (e.g. with a default object that holds the default values for the font)</p></div>'},  {'from': 'human', 'value': 'Add a font weight of 400px'},  {'from': 'gpt', 'value': '<div class="markdown prose w-full break-words dark:prose-invert light"><p>You can add a font weight of 400px to the <code>CustomDiv</code> component using the <code>font-weight</code> property in the CSS. Here is an example of how you can do this:</p><pre><div class="bg-black mb-4 rounded-md"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><button class="flex ml-auto gap-2"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M16 4h2a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v14a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H6a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V6a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h2"></path><rect x="8" y="2" width="8" height="4" rx="1" ry="1"></rect></svg>Copy code</button></div><div class="p-4 overflow-y-auto"><code class="!whitespace-pre-wrap hljs language-javascript"><span class="hljs-keyword">import</span> styled <span class="hljs-keyword">from</span> <span class="hljs-string">'styled-components'</span>;

<span class="hljs-keyword">const</span> fontStyles = {
  <span class="hljs-attr">typography</span>: {
    <span class="hljs-attr">primary</span>: {
      <span class="hljs-attr">display</span>: <span class="hljs-string">'mnsLondonRegular'</span>,
      <span class="hljs-attr">semiBold</span>: <span class="hljs-string">'mnsLondonBold'</span>
    }
  }
}

<span class="hljs-keyword">const</span> <span class="hljs-title class_">CustomDiv</span> = styled.<span class="hljs-property">div</span><span class="hljs-string">`
  font-family: <span class="hljs-subst">${fontStyles.typography.primary.display || <span class="hljs-string">'sans-serif'</span>}</span>;
  font-weight: 400;
`</span>;

<span class="hljs-keyword">function</span> <span class="hljs-title function_">MyComponent</span>(<span class="hljs-params"></span>) {
  <span class="hljs-keyword">return</span> <span class="xml"><span class="hljs-tag">&lt;<span class="hljs-name">CustomDiv</span>&gt;</span>This text has a custom font.<span class="hljs-tag">&lt;/<span class="hljs-name">CustomDiv</span>&gt;</span></span>;
}
</code></div></div></pre><p>In this example, the <code>font-weight</code> property is set to <code>400</code> which will set the font weight to normal. The font weight value is in a scale of 100-900, where 100 is the thinnest and 900 is the thickest. So 400 is the normal font-weight.</p><p>You can also use keywords instead of numeric values for font-weight property.</p><pre><div class="bg-black mb-4 rounded-md"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><button class="flex ml-auto gap-2"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M16 4h2a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v14a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H6a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V6a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h2"></path><rect x="8" y="2" width="8" height="4" rx="1" ry="1"></rect></svg>Copy code</button></div><div class="p-4 overflow-y-auto"><code class="!whitespace-pre-wrap hljs language-javascript"><span class="hljs-keyword">const</span> <span class="hljs-title class_">CustomDiv</span> = styled.<span class="hljs-property">div</span><span class="hljs-string">`
  font-family: <span class="hljs-subst">${fontStyles.typography.primary.display || <span class="hljs-string">'sans-serif'</span>}</span>;
