t', 'value': '<div><p>In Azure SQL Database, it is not possible to override password complexity requirements only for a certain database on a server. The password policy settings are applied at the server level, which means that all databases on the server are subject to the same password policy.</p><p>If you need to have different password policies for different databases, you may want to consider creating separate servers for each database. This approach would allow you to configure different password policies for each server, which in turn would apply to the databases hosted on that server.</p><p>Alternatively, you could consider using Active Directory authentication for your Azure SQL Database. With Active Directory authentication, you can use the password policy settings that are configured in your Active Directory domain, which would allow you to have different password policies for different user accounts, including those used to access your Azure SQL Database.</p></div>'},  {'from': 'human', 'value': 'according to microsoft:
