ssword that does not meet the complexity requirements of the password policy, you can create the user without specifying a password, and then reset the password to a value that meets the password policy requirements.</p><p>Here is an example SQL query that creates a user without specifying a password and then resets the password to 'mypassword123', which meets the default password policy requirements:</p><pre><div class="bg-black mb-4 rounded-md"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><span>sql</span><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"></svg>Copy code</div><div><code class="!whitespace-pre hljs language-sql"><span class="hljs-keyword">CREATE</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">USER</span> [myuser];
<span class="hljs-keyword">ALTER</span> LOGIN [myuser] <span class="hljs-keyword">WITH</span> PASSWORD <span class="hljs-operator">=</span> <span class="hljs-string">'mypassword123'</span>;
</code></div></div></pre><p>Note that if the password policy has been explicitly configured to enforce specific complexity requirements, you will need to specify a password that meets those requirements when you create or reset the user password.</p></div>'},  {'from': 'human', 'value': 'tell me about how I can change the password complixity on an azure sql server'},  {'from': 'gpt', 'value': '<div><p>In Azure SQL Database, you can configure the password complexity requirements using the Azure portal, PowerShell, or Azure CLI. By default, Azure SQL Database requires passwords to have at least 8 characters and meet password complexity requirements, such as including uppercase and lowercase letters, numbers, and symbols.</p><p>To change the password complexity requirements in Azure SQL Database using the Azure portal, follow these steps:</p><ol><li>Navigate to the server that hosts your Azure SQL Database in the Azure portal.</li><li>Under the "Security + networking" section, select "Firewalls and virtual networks".</li><li>Under "Security", select "Password policy".</li><li>Modify the password policy settings as desired, including the minimum password length, required character types (such as uppercase letters, lowercase letters, numbers, and symbols), and the number of previous passwords that cannot be reused.</li><li>Select "Save" to apply the new password policy settings.</li></ol><p>To change the password complexity requirements using PowerShell or Azure CLI, you can use the Set-AzSqlServerPasswordPolicy or az sql server ad-admin set commands, respectively. Here is an example PowerShell command that sets the minimum password length to 10 characters and requires at least one uppercase letter, one lowercase letter, and one digit:</p><pre><div class="bg-black mb-4 rounded-md"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><span>powershell</span><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"></svg>Copy code</div><div><code class="!whitespace-pre hljs language-powershell">Set-AzSqlServerPasswordPolicy -ResourceGroupName "myresourcegroup" -ServerName "myserver" -MinimumPasswordLength 10 -PasswordRequireUppercase Enabled -PasswordRequireLowercase Enabled -PasswordRequireDigit Enabled
</code></div></div></pre><p>Note that changing the password complexity requirements may not be compliant with some security standards and best practices, and you should carefully consider the implications of making these changes before doing so.</p></div>'}]

[ {'from': 'human', 'value': 'asp.net,vue,httponly,JWTtokencookie'},  {'from': 'gpt', 'value': '<div class="markdown prose w-full break-words dark:prose-invert dark"><p> ASP.NET  Vue.js, HttpOnly  JWT Token  Cookie ,:</p><ol><li><p> ASP.NET  JWT Token, Token  HttpOnly JavaScript  Cookie</p></li><li><p> Token  Cookie , Secure  HttpOnlySecure  Cookie  HTTPS ,</p></li><li><p> Vue.js , JavaScript  Cookie , js-cookie, Cookie  JWT Token</p></li><li><p> Token , Authorization Header ,:Authorization: Bearer {token}</p></li><li><p> ASP.NET , Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.JwtBearer  JWT Token, Token </p></li></ol><p>, JWT Token  HttpOnly  Secure  Cookie ,</p></div>'},  {'from': 'human', 'value': '13'},  {'from': 'gpt', 'value': '<div class="markdown prose w-full break-words dark:prose-invert dark"><p>, JWT Token  HttpOnly  Secure  Cookie :</p><ol><li> ASP.NET :</li></ol><p> ASP.NET  JwtSecurityTokenHandler  JWT Token, Token  HttpOnly:</p><pre><div class="bg-black mb-4 rounded-md"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><span class="">csharp</span><button class="flex ml-auto gap-2"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M16 4h2a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v14a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H6a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V6a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h2"></path><rect x="8" y="2" width="8" height="4" rx="1" ry="1"></rect></svg>Copy code</button></div><div class="p-4 overflow-y-auto"><code class="!whitespace-pre hljs language-csharp"><span class="hljs-keyword">var</span> tokenHandler = <span class="hljs-keyword">new</span> JwtSecurityTokenHandler();
<span class="hljs-keyword">var</span> key = Encoding.ASCII.GetBytes(<span class="hljs-string">"your_secret_key"</span>);
<span class="hljs-keyword">var</span> tokenDescriptor = <span class="hljs-keyword">new</span> SecurityTokenDescriptor
{
    Subject = <span class="hljs-keyword">new</span> ClaimsIdentity(<span class="hljs-keyword">new</span> Claim[]
    {
        <span class="hljs-keyword">new</span> Claim(ClaimTypes.Name, <span class="hljs-string">"John Doe"</span>),
        <span class="hljs-keyword">new</span> Claim(ClaimTypes.Email, <span class="hljs-string">"johndoe@example.com"</span>)
    }),
    Expires = DateTime.UtcNow.AddMinutes(<span class="hljs-number">30</span>),
    SigningCredentials = <span class="hljs-keyword">new</span> SigningCredentials(<span class="hljs-keyword">new</span> SymmetricSecurityKey(key), SecurityAlgorithms.HmacSha256Signature)
};
<span class="hljs-keyword">var</span> token = tokenHandler.CreateToken(tokenDescriptor);

<span class="hljs-keyword">var</span> tokenString = tokenHandler.WriteToken(token);

<span class="hljs-comment">// Set the token as a HttpOnly cookie</span>
HttpContext.Response.Cookies.Append(<span class="hljs-string">"access_token"</span>, tokenString, <span class="hljs-keyword">new</span> CookieOptions
{
    HttpOnly = <span class="hljs-literal">true</span>,
    Secure = <span class="hljs-literal">true</span>,
    SameSite = SameSiteMode.Strict
});
</code></div></div></pre><ol start="2"><li> Vue.js :</li></ol><p> Vue.js  js-cookie , Cookie  JWT Token:</p><pre><div class="bg-black mb-4 rounded-md"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><span class="">javascript</span><button class="flex ml-auto gap-2"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M16 4h2a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v14a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H6a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V6a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h2"></path><rect x="8" y="2" width="8" height="4" rx="1" ry="1"></rect></svg>Copy code</button></div><div class="p-4 overflow-y-auto"><code class="!whitespace-pre hljs language-javascript"><span class="hljs-keyword">import</span> <span class="hljs-title class_">Cookies</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">from</span> <span class="hljs-string">'js-cookie'</span>

<span class="hljs-keyword">const</span> token = <span class="hljs-title class_">Cookies</span>.<span class="hljs-title function_">get</span>(<span class="hljs-string">'access_token'</span>)
</code></div></div></pre><ol start="3"><li>ASP.NET  JWT Token:</li></ol><p> ASP.NET  Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.JwtBearer  JWT Token:</p><pre><div class="bg-black mb-4 rounded-md"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><span class="">csharp</span><button class="flex ml-auto gap-2"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M16 4h2a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v14a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H6a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V6a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h2"></path><rect x="8" y="2" width="8" height="4" rx="1" ry="1"></rect></svg>Copy code</button></div><div class="p-4 overflow-y-auto"><code class="!whitespace-pre hljs language-csharp"><span class="hljs-function"><span class="hljs-keyword">public</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">void</span> <span class="hljs-title">ConfigureServices</span>(<span class="hljs-params">IServiceCollection services</span>)</span>
{
    services.AddAuthentication(JwtBearerDefaults.AuthenticationScheme)
        .AddJwtBearer(options =&gt;
        {
            options.RequireHttpsMetadata = <span class="hljs-literal">true</span>;
            options.SaveToken = <span class="hljs-literal">true</span>;
            options.TokenValidationParameters = <span class="hljs-keyword">new</span> TokenValidationParameters
            {
                ValidateIssuerSigningKey = <span class="hljs-literal">true</span>,
                IssuerSigningKey = <span class="hljs-keyword">new</span> SymmetricSecurityKey(Encoding.ASCII.GetBytes(<span class="hljs-string">"your_secret_key"</span>)),
                ValidateIssuer = <span class="hljs-literal">false</span>,
                ValidateAudience = <span class="hljs-literal">false</span>
            };
        });
}

