"},  {'from': 'gpt', 'value': "<div><p>This data model represents an attack graph for simulating a network attack scenario using the attackiq platform. The scenario consists of three steps: network discovery, lateral movement using SSH, and system information discovery.</p><p>The main components of this data model include:</p><ol><li>TTL (Time to Live): 6000000</li><li>Name: MTAG - Network Discovery leads to Lateral Movement using Secure Shell (SSH)</li><li>Type: maag (multi-asset attack graph)</li><li>Graph: Contains the nodes (steps) of the attack graph with their properties<ul><li>Node 0: Network discovery using a SYN scan on TCP ports 22 and 2222</li><li>Node 1: Lateral movement using SSH with a specific RSA private key and user 'ubuntu' on port 22</li><li>Node 2: System information discovery using platform-specific scripts (Windows or Linux)</li></ul></li><li>Version: 2</li><li>Assigned_user_privileges: false</li></ol><p>In this attack graph, an attacker first performs a network discovery scan to find remote systems with common SSH ports open (Node 0). After finding a vulnerable system, the attacker uses SSH to laterally move within the network (Node 1) and execute the 'whoami' command. Finally, the attacker performs system information discovery (Node 2) by running platform-specific scripts on the compromised system to gather more information.</p><p>The data model also contains information about the position of the nodes, test points, scenario IDs, scenario names, and other parameters used in the simulation.</p></div>"},  {'from': 'human', 'value': 'This the example of the mitre attack flow data model


