}'},  {'from': 'gpt', 'value': "<div><p>The JSON schema provided is for the Attack Flow STIX 2.1 Extension. The schema extends STIX with additional STIX Data Objects (SDOs) that model Attack Flow concepts. It includes various SDOs such as attack-flow, attack-action, attack-asset, attack-condition, and attack-operator.</p><ol><li><p>attack-flow: This object contains metadata for the name and description of the attack flow, starting points for the flow of actions, and can be referenced from other STIX objects.</p></li><li><p>attack-action: Represents the execution of a particular technique or a discrete unit of adversary behavior. It includes properties such as tactic_id, tactic_ref, technique_id, technique_ref, description, execution_start, execution_end, command_ref, asset_refs, and effect_refs.</p></li><li><p>attack-asset: Represents an object that is the subject or target of an action. Assets can be technical or non-technical, such as machines, data, people, or physical systems. The object has properties like name, description, and object_ref.</p></li><li><p>attack-condition: Represents some possible condition, outcome, or state that could occur. Conditions are used to split flows based on the success or failure of an action or to provide further description of an action's results. The object includes properties such as description, pattern, pattern_type, pattern_version, on_true_refs, and on_false_refs.</p></li><li><p>attack-operator: Joins multiple attack paths together using boolean logic. It has properties like operator and effect_refs.</p></li></ol><p>The schema has several other properties and requirements for each of the objects, including spec_version, type, and specific constraints for various properties. It also provides examples of each object type.</p></div>"},  {'from': 'human', 'value': 'Take the stab at converting the tesla breach attack flow to attackiq attack graph yaml'},  {'from': 'gpt', 'value': '<div><p>Based on the Tesla breach attack flow pr