  });
</code></div></div></pre><p>This code reads the text content of the clipboard using the <code>navigator.clipboard.readText()</code> method and logs it to the console. Note that this API requires the user's permission to access the clipboard, and it only works in the context of a user gesture, such as a mouse click or a keyboard event.</p></div>'},  {'from': 'human', 'value': 'is there a "clipboardRead" permission in v3?'},  {'from': 'gpt', 'value': '<div class="markdown prose w-full break-words dark:prose-invert light"><p>No, the <code>clipboardRead</code> permission is not available in manifest v3.</p><p>Manifest v3 introduces a new permission model that replaces the previous permission system in manifest v2. The new permission model aims to provide more fine-grained control over the APIs that an extension can access, and it does not include the <code>clipboardRead</code> permission.</p><p>In manifest v3, the clipboard can still be accessed using the <code>navigator.clipboard</code> API, as I mentioned in my previous response. However, this API requires a different permission called <code>clipboardWrite</code>, which allows an extension to write data to the clipboard.</p><p>Here's an example of how to request the <code>clipboardWrite</code> permission in the manifest.json file:</p><pre><div class="bg-black mb-4 rounded-md"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><span class="">json</span><button class="flex ml-auto gap-2"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M16 4h2a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v14a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H6a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V6a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h2"></path><rect x="8" y="2" width="8" height="4" rx="1" ry="1"></rect></svg>Copy code</button></div><div class="p-4 overflow-y-auto"><code class="!whitespace-pre hljs language-json"><span class="hljs-punctuation">{</span>
  <span class="hljs-attr">"name"</span><span class="hljs-punctuation">:</span> <span class="hljs-string">"My Extension"</span><span class="hljs-punctuation">,</span>
  <span class="hljs-attr">"version"</span><span class="hljs-punctuation">:</span> <span class="hljs-string">"1.0"</span><span class="hljs-punctuation">,</span>
  <span class="hljs-attr">"manifest_version"</span><span class="hljs-punctuation">:</span> <span class="hljs-number">3</span><span class="hljs-punctuation">,</span>
  <span class="hljs-attr">"permissions"</span><span class="hljs-punctuation">:</span> <span class="hljs-punctuation">[</span>
    <span class="hljs-string">"clipboardWrite"</span>
  <span class="hljs-punctuation">]</span><span class="hljs-punctuation">,</span>
  <span class="hljs-attr">"background"</span><span class="hljs-punctuation">:</span> <span class="hljs-punctuation">{</span>
