[ {'From': 'Human', 'Value': 'I'm writing a MPB music mixed with pop. The letter E thus: \ n \ n "wakes up, but it can be without hurry \ nla Outside the day starts early \ ne we have nothing to lose \ ne here the time slows \ ne never regret losing this time with you \ nacorda and is a little more \ \ knows that I am crazy \ ne and here that we will understand \ nnao? In me \ n --- Refrao --- \ nentao leaves "\ n \ ncontinue the letter '}, {'From': 'GPT', 'VALUE': '<Div Class = "Markdown Prose W-Full Break-Words Dark: Prose-Invert Light"> <p> Let the life go, let the love flow, let the heart beat \ nnao we need nothing more, just being together \ ne everything I need, and everything I need I want the music to play, let dreams happen \ Neu I want to live this life by your side, always \ nentao leaves, let everything be natural \ Neu promise that I will take care of you, always. "</p> </div>}, {'From': 'Human', 'Value': 'Continue the letter from here: \ n \ n "wakes up, but it can be without hurry \ nla starts the day starts early \ ne we have nothing to lose \ ne here the time slows"'}, {'From': 'GPT', 'VALUE': '<Div Class = "Markdown Prose W-Full Break-Words Dark: Prose-Invert Light"> <p> I want to enjoy every second \ ncom you by my side, I feel that everything is possible \ nnao matters what the world tells us, I know that it is true \ in this love and strong and strong True </p> --- Refrao --- \ nentao lets, let the sun come in \ ndexes the life roll, let love flow \ nnao we need nothing more, just being together \ ne everything I need, and everything I want </p> <p> Let's live as if it were the last \ ne Nego I promise to love you always \ nentao Leave it, let it all be natural \ Neu promise that I will take care of you, always. "</p> </div>}, {'From': 'Human', 'Value': 'Routine and Consistency in Programming'}, {'From': 'GPT', 'Value': '<Div Class = "Markdown Prose W-Full Break-Words Dark: Prose-Invert Light"> <p> Routine and Consistency are fundamental in programming. The routine refers to the creation of habits and procedures that help maintain the productivity and quality of the code. This includes things like maintaining a regular working time, doing frequent testing, and using source code management tools. This includes things like following a consistent coding style, consistently appoint variables and functions, and follow design patterns. This helps ensure that the code is easy to read and maintain. </p> <p> Maintaining a routine and consistency helps ensure that the code is of high quality, easy to understand and maintain, and that errors are easier to find and correct. In addition, it helps to ensure that the project is completed within the time and within the orcament. {'From': 'Human', 'VALUE': 'Set up a separated study routine per time that aims to study in the Kotlin Android programming. Remembering that work from 8hrs to 18hrs. '}, {'From': 'GPT', 'Value': '<Div Class = "Markdown Prose W-Full Break-Words Dark: Prose-Invert Light"> <P> a possible study routine for studying Kotlin for Android could be: </p> <p> 6h00-Wake up and make a rapid review of the previous day notes. H30 - Exercise and solve problems related to Kotlin. </p> <p> 7h30 - take breakfast and prepare for work. N and ANDROID DEVELOPMENT. Adapt the routine according to your needs and availability. It is also important to maintain a healthy balance between study and leisure. </p> </div>}, {'From': 'Human', 'Value': 'Adapt the routine for the following tasks - I wake up at 6:00 am and go to the gym at 6:20 am, I will sleep at 11:45 pm}, {'From': 'GPT', 'VALUE': '<Div Class = "Markdown Prose W-Full Break-Words Dark: Prose-Invert Light"> <p> A Possible Study Routine Adapted to include Academy can be: </p> <p> 6h00-Wake up and prepare to go to the academy. </p> <p> 7h30 - take breakfast and prepare for work. </p> <p> 8h00 - Working from 8am to 6pm. Make practical exercises and projects related to Kotlin and Android Development. </p> <p> 23h00 - Review the notes and prepare for the next day. . It is also important to maintain a healthy balance between study, work, physical exercises and leisure. {'From': 'Human', 'VALUE': 'Help me with simple Android project ideas but very useful, such as calculators, name generators (video games)'}, {'From': 'GPT', 'VALUE': '<Div Class = "Markdown Prose W-Full Break-Words Dark: Prose-Invert Light"> <p> Some simple but very useful project ideas, include: </p> <l> <l> <p> Financial calculator: an application that allows user to calculate composite interest, interest, Amortization of loan and other common financial operations. Users, can be used for games or profiles on social networks. </p> </li> <p> Task Manager: An application that allows user to create and manage task lists, reminders and appointments. HEALTH. Recipes: An application that allows user to search and save recipes, and add ingredients to a shopping list. The important thing is to think of something you think would be useful and that you would be interested in developing. </p> </div> '}, {'From': 'Human', 'VALUE': 'Based on open research that make available the quantities of research on platforms like Google and Admob, what would be the ideas of utilitarian application?'}, {'From': 'GPT', 'VALUE': '<Div Class = "Markdown Prose W-Full Break-Words Dark: Prose-Invert Light"> <p> Based on Utility Application Ideas that have a high demand include: </p> <li> <p> Password Application: An application that stores and manages Passwords safely and easy to use. JPG. ​​</p> </li> <li> <p> Task Management Application: An application that allows user to create and manage task lists, reminders and appointments. File Management: An application that allows user to manage files and folders on your device. Device. Remember that it is always important to do your own research and check the demand and competence before starting the development of an application. {'From': 'Human', 'VALUE': 'I have an API in Nodejs, I need to take the data data data and convert to string before sending to the application: {"id": {"type": "buffer", "date": [50.48.48.48.48.48]}'}, {'from': 'gpt', 'value': '<div class="markdown prose w-full break-words dark:prose-invert light"><p>Para converter o campo "data" em um objeto JSON em formato de string, voce pode usar o metodo JSON.stringify(). Ele ira retornar uma string JSON a partir de um objeto ou valor.</p><p>Exemplo:</p><pre><div class="bg-black mb-4 rounded-md"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><span class="">javascript</span><button class="flex ml-auto gap-2"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M16 4h2a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v14a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H6a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V6a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h2"></path><rect x="8" y="2" width="8" height="4" rx="1" ry="1"></rect></svg>Copy code</button></div><div class="p-4 overflow-y-auto"><code class="!whitespace-pre hljs language-javascript"><span class="hljs-keyword">const</span> data = {<span class="hljs-string">"ID"</span>:{<span class="hljs-string">"type"</span>:<span class="hljs-string">"Buffer"</span>,<span class="hljs-string">"data"</span>:[<span class="hljs-number">50</span>,<span class="hljs-number">48</span>,<span class="hljs-number">48</span>,<span class="hljs-number">53</span>,<span class="hljs-number">50</span>,<span class="hljs-number">48</span>,<span class="hljs-number">48</span>,<span class="hljs-number">48</span>]}};
