    <span class="hljs-comment">// loop body</span>
}
</code></div></div></pre><p>The <code>datatype</code> specifies the data type of the elements in the collection. The <code>variable</code> is the name of a new variable that will be created for each iteration of the loop, which will hold the value of the current element in the collection. The <code>collection</code> is the array or collection that you want to iterate over.</p><p>Here's an example of how to use the <code>foreach</code> loop with an array:</p><pre><div class="bg-black rounded-md mb-4"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><span>java</span><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"></svg>Copy code</div><div><code class="!whitespace-pre hljs language-java"><span class="hljs-type">int</span>[] numbers = {<span class="hljs-number">1</span>, <span class="hljs-number">2</span>, <span class="hljs-number">3</span>, <span class="hljs-number">4</span>, <span class="hljs-number">5</span>};

<span class="hljs-keyword">for</span> (<span class="hljs-type">int</span> num : numbers) {
