e 66, 'C' has code 67, and so on). This code scheme is used to represent characters in many computer systems and programming languages.</p></div>"},  {'from': 'human', 'value': 'Throw exception in java'},  {'from': 'gpt', 'value': '<div><p>In Java, exceptions can be thrown using the <code>throw</code> keyword followed by an instance of a class that extends the <code>Throwable</code> class. Here's an example of how to throw an exception:</p><pre><div class="bg-black rounded-md mb-4"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><span>java</span><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"></svg>Copy code</div><div><code class="!whitespace-pre hljs language-java"><span class="hljs-keyword">public</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">void</span> <span class="hljs-title function_">divide</span><span class="hljs-params">(<span class="hljs-type">int</span> dividend, <span class="hljs-type">int</span> divisor)</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">throws</span> ArithmeticException {
