    System.out.println(<span class="hljs-string">"Result: "</span> + result);
}
</code></div></div></pre><p>In the above code, the <code>divide</code> method takes two integer arguments, <code>dividend</code> and <code>divisor</code>. If the <code>divisor</code> is 0, an <code>ArithmeticException</code> is thrown with a message "Division by zero!". Otherwise, the method performs integer division and prints the result.</p><p>When you call this method, you need to handle the exception by either catching it or declaring that the method itself throws the exception. Here's an example of catching the exception:</p><pre><div class="bg-black rounded-md mb-4"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><span>java</span><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"></svg>Copy code</div><div><code class="!whitespace-pre hljs language-java"><span class="hljs-keyword">try</span> {
