act audit should include a review of the contract's code to ensure that it does not allow for unsecured upgrades. This can be done manually by a skilled auditor, or automated tools such as Mythril or Oyente can be used to help identify potential vulnerabilities. Additionally, testing the contract on a test network and simulating potential attacks can also help catch this vulnerability.</p></div>'},  {'from': 'human', 'value': 'give the vulnerbility a tittle'},  {'from': 'gpt', 'value': '<div class="request-:R3d6:-15 markdown prose break-words dark:prose-invert light"><p>The vulnerability in the contract <code>VRFNFTRandomDrawFactory</code> where the owner can upgrade the contract implementation without additional security measures can be titled "Unsecured contract upgrade vulnerability". This vulnerability allows an attacker who gains control of the owner's account to potentially compromise the contract and steal funds or NFTs.</p></div>'},  {'from': 'human', 'value': 'show proof of concept in that vulnerbility'},  {'from': 'gpt', 'value': '<div class="request-:R3d6:-16 markdown prose break-words dark:prose-invert light"><p>To demonstrate the unsecured contract upgrade vulnerability in the <code>VRFNFTRandomDrawFactory</code> contract, we can simulate the following scenario:</p><ol><li>An attacker gains control of the contract owner's account.</li><li>The attacker uses the contract's <code>_authorizeUpgrade()</code> function to upgrade the contract implementation to a malicious or vulnerable implementation.</li><li>The attacker then uses the newly upgraded contract to steal funds or NFTs from the contract.</li></ol><p>This scenario demonstrates how an attacker can exploit the unsecured contract upgrade vulnerability in the <code>VRFNFTRandomDrawFactory</code> contract to compromise the contract and steal funds or NFTs. To prevent this vulnerability, the contract should be modified to prevent the owner from upgrading the contract implementation without additional security measures, such as a timelock or multisig.</p></div>'}]

