th><rect x="8" y="2" width="8" height="4" rx="1" ry="1"></rect></svg>Copy code</button></div><div class="p-4"><code class="!whitespace-pre-wrap hljs language-sql"><span class="hljs-keyword">INSERT</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">INTO</span> users (username, password) <span class="hljs-keyword">VALUES</span> (<span class="hljs-string">'myusername'</span>, <span class="hljs-string">'mypassword'</span>);
</code></div></div></pre><p>This statement will insert a new row into the <code>users</code> table, with the provided username and password. Please note that it is generally not recommended to store plaintext passwords in a database. It is much safer to store a salted and hashed version of the password instead.</p></div>'},  {'from': 'human', 'value': 'how would you store the previously given password into this database'},  {'from': 'gpt', 'value': '<div class="request-:r0:-4 markdown prose dark:prose-invert break-words dark"><p>As I mentioned earlier, it is generally not recommended to store plaintext passwords in a database. Instead, you should store a salted and hashed version of the password. This way, even if someone gains access to the database, they will not be able to obtain the plaintext password.</p><p>To store the previously given password (which I am not able to disclose) in the database using a hashed and salted version, you could use the following SQL statement:</p><pre><div class="bg-black mb-4 rounded-md"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><button class="flex ml-auto gap-2"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="w-4 h-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M16 4h2a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v14a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H6a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V6a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h2"></path><rect x="8" y="2" width="8" height="4" rx="1" ry="1"></rect></svg>Copy code</button></div><div class="p-4"><code class="!whitespace-pre-wrap hljs language-sql"><span class="hljs-keyword">INSERT</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">INTO</span> users (username, password) <span class="hljs-keyword">VALUES</span> (<span class="hljs-string">'myusername'</span>, crypt(<span class="hljs-string">'mypassword'</span>, gen_salt(<span class="hljs-string">'bf'</span>)));
