 are many resources available online, such as documentation, tutorials, and open-source code, that can help you get started without spending a lot of money.</p></div>'},  {'from': 'human', 'value': 'can you provide code for 3 '},  {'from': 'gpt', 'value': '<div><p>Sure, here's an example of a simple smart contract written in Solidity, the programming language used for Ethereum:</p><pre><div class="bg-black rounded-md mb-4"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><span>csharp</span><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"></svg>Copy code</div><div><code class="!whitespace-pre hljs language-csharp"><span class="hljs-comment">// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT</span>

