</code></div></div></pre><ol start="2"><li>Use an alternative method of reading the file that doesn't require reading it all into memory at once. For example, you could use <code>fgets()</code> to read the file line by line, or <code>getc()</code> to read the file character by character. Here's an example of how the code could be modified to use <code>fgets()</code>:</li></ol><pre><div class="bg-black mb-4 rounded-md"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><span class="">c</span><button class="flex ml-auto gap-2"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M16 4h2a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v14a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H6a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V6a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h2"></path><rect x="8" y="2" width="8" height="4" rx="1" ry="1"></rect></svg>Copy code</button></div><div class="p-4 overflow-y-auto"><code class="!whitespace-pre hljs language-c"><span class="hljs-meta">#<span class="hljs-keyword">include</span> <span class="hljs-string">&lt;stdio.h&gt;</span></span>
<span class="hljs-meta">#<span class="hljs-keyword">include</span> <span class="hljs-string">&lt;stdlib.h&gt;</span></span>
<span class="hljs-meta">#<span class="hljs-keyword">include</span> <span class="hljs-string">&lt;string.h&gt;</span></span>

<span class="hljs-meta">#<span class="hljs-keyword">define</span> LINE_SIZE 1024</span>

<span class="hljs-type">int</span> <span class="hljs-title function_">main</span><span class="hljs-params">(<span class="hljs-type">int</span> argc, <span class="hljs-type">char</span> *argv[])</span> {
    <span class="hljs-type">char</span> *filename = argv[<span class="hljs-number">1</span>];
    FILE *file = fopen(filename, <span class="hljs-string">"r"</span>);
    <span class="hljs-type">char</span> *line = <span class="hljs-literal">NULL</span>;
    <span class="hljs-type">size_t</span> lineLen = <span class="hljs-number">0</span>;
    <span class="hljs-type">ssize_t</span> bytesRead;

    <span class="hljs-keyword">if</span> (file == <span class="hljs-literal">NULL</span>) {
        <span class="hljs-built_in">fprintf</span>(<span class="hljs-built_in">stderr</span>, <span class="hljs-string">"Error opening file\n"</span>);
        <span class="hljs-keyword">return</span> <span class="hljs-number">1</span>;
    }

    <span class="hljs-keyword">while</span> ((bytesRead = getline(&amp;line, &amp;lineLen, file)) != <span class="hljs-number">-1</span>) {
        <span class="hljs-comment">// Do some processing on the line</span>
    }

    fclose(file);
    <span class="hljs-built_in">free</span>(line);

    <span class="hljs-keyword">return</span> <span class="hljs-number">0</span>;
}
</code></div></div></pre><p>In this version of the code, <code>getline()</code> reads the file line by line, and each line is processed separately. This approach avoids the need to read the entire file into memory at once, and therefore eliminates the risk of a <code>malloc()</code> failure due to lack of memory. Note that the <code>line</code> buffer is allocated dynamically by <code>getline()</code>, and must be freed with <code>free()</code> after the file is closed.</p></div>'}]

[ {'from': 'human', 'value': 'I want to  access my password from  CyberArk Identity and Security and Access Management  from   my ASP .NET backend server. I want to get the whole code and steps for the process to execute the same including to create a test account in CyberArk.'},  {'from': 'gpt', 'value': '<div><p>To access your password from CyberArk Identity and Security and Access Management from your ASP.NET backend server, you can follow these steps:</p><ol><li>Create a test account in CyberArk:</li></ol><ul><li>Sign up for a CyberArk account (if you don't have one) at <a href="https://www.cyberark.com/" target="_new">https://www.cyberark.com/</a>.</li><li>Create a new safe and add a new secret (username and password) that you want to access from your ASP.NET backend server.</li></ul><ol><li>Set up CyberArk REST API:</li></ol><p>CyberArk provides a REST API to interact with its services. You need to enable and configure the REST API to access the secret from your application.</p><ul><li>Log in to the CyberArk Web Portal.</li><li>Follow the CyberArk documentation to enable and configure the REST API: <a href="https://docs.cyberark.com/Product-Doc/OnlineHelp/PAS/Latest/en/Content/SDK/Central-Credential-Provider-REST-API.htm" target="_new">https://docs.cyberark.com/Product-Doc/OnlineHelp/PAS/Latest/en/Content/SDK/Central-Credential-Provider-REST-API.htm</a></li></ul><ol><li>Create an ASP.NET backend server:</li></ol><p>Create a new ASP.NET project in Visual Studio, or use an existing one. If you need to create a new project, you can follow these steps:</p><ul><li>Open Visual Studio.</li><li>Click on "Create a new project."</li><li>Select "ASP.NET Web Application (.NET Framework)" and click "Next."</li><li>Enter a name for your project and click "Create."</li><li>Choose a template, such as "Empty" or "Web API," and click "Create."</li></ul><ol><li>Install the necessary NuGet packages:</li></ol><p>Install the Newtonsoft.Json package to help with JSON parsing and handling:</p><ul><li>In Visual Studio, right-click on your project and click on "Manage NuGet Packages."</li><li>Click on "Browse" and search for "Newtonsoft.Json."</li><li>Install the Newtonsoft.Json package.</li></ul><ol><li>Add the following code to your ASP.NET backend server:</li></ol><p>Create a new class, for example, <code>CyberArkClient.cs</code>, and add the following code to handle the communication with the CyberArk REST API:</p><pre><div class="bg-black rounded-md mb-4"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><span>csharp</span><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"></svg>Copy code</div><div><code class="!whitespace-pre hljs language-csharp"><span class="hljs-keyword">using</span> System;
<span class="hljs-keyword">using</span> System.IO;
<span class="hljs-keyword">using</span> System.Net;
<span class="hljs-keyword">using</span> System.Text;
<span class="hljs-keyword">using</span> Newtonsoft.Json;

<span class="hljs-keyword">public</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">class</span> <span class="hljs-title">CyberArkClient</span>
{
    <span class="hljs-keyword">private</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">readonly</span> <span class="hljs-built_in">string</span> _baseUrl;
    <span class="hljs-keyword">private</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">readonly</span> <span class="hljs-built_in">string</span> _apiUsername;
    <span class="hljs-keyword">private</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">readonly</span> <span class="hljs-built_in">string</span> _apiPassword;

    <span class="hljs-function"><span class="hljs-keyword">public</span> <span class="hljs-title">CyberArkClient</span>(<span class="hljs-params"><span class="hljs-built_in">string</span> baseUrl, <span class="hljs-built_in">string</span> apiUsername, <span class="hljs-built_in">string</span> apiPassword</span>)</span>
    {
        _baseUrl = baseUrl;
        _apiUsername = apiUsername;
        _apiPassword = apiPassword;
    }

    <span class="hljs-function"><span class="hljs-keyword">public</span> <span class="hljs-built_in">string</span> <span class="hljs-title">GetPassword</span>(<span class="hljs-params"><span class="hljs-built_in">string</span> safeName, <span class="hljs-built_in">string</span> secretName</span>)</span>
    {
        <span class="hljs-keyword">var</span> token = GetAuthToken();
