[ {'from': 'human', 'value': 'How would I use bcrypt for password storage on FreeRTOS? I have an STM32 microcontroller running FreeRTOS'},  {'from': 'gpt', 'value': '<div class="markdown prose w-full break-words dark:prose-invert light"><p>To use bcrypt for password storage on FreeRTOS, you would need to find a C implementation of bcrypt that is compatible with your STM32 microcontroller. Here are the steps you can follow:</p><ol><li><p>Find a bcrypt library: First, you need to find a bcrypt library that is compatible with your STM32 microcontroller and FreeRTOS. You can search for an existing implementation online or develop your own implementation.</p></li><li><p>Integrate the library into your project: Once you have a bcrypt library, you will need to integrate it into your project. This will typically involve adding the library files to your project and linking against them.</p></li><li><p>Hash the password: To hash a password using bcrypt, you will need to call the bcrypt function with the password and a randomly generated salt. The salt should be stored along with the hashed password so that it can be used to verify the password later.</p></li><li><p>Verify the password: To verify a password using bcrypt, you will need to retrieve the hashed password and salt from storage, and then call the bcrypt function again with the candidate password and the retrieved salt. If the resulting hash matches the stored hash, then the password is valid.</p></li></ol><p>Here is an example code snippet to hash a password using the popular bcrypt library called <code>bcrypt-crypt</code>:</p><pre><div class="bg-black mb-4 rounded-md"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><span class="">scss</span><button class="flex ml-auto gap-2"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M16 4h2a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v14a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H6a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V6a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h2"></path><rect x="8" y="2" width="8" height="4" rx="1" ry="1"></rect></svg>Copy code</button></div><div class="p-4 overflow-y-auto"><code class="!whitespace-pre hljs language-scss"><span class="hljs-selector-id">#include</span> "bcrypt/bcrypt<span class="hljs-selector-class">.h</span>"

void <span class="hljs-built_in">hash_password</span>(const char *password) {
  char hashed_password<span class="hljs-selector-attr">[BCRYPT_HASHSIZE]</span>;
  char salt<span class="hljs-selector-attr">[BCRYPT_MAXSALT]</span>;

  <span class="hljs-comment">// generate a random salt</span>
  <span class="hljs-built_in">bcrypt_gensalt</span>(<span class="hljs-number">12</span>, salt);

  <span class="hljs-comment">// hash the password with the salt</span>
