Fix: Use the Checks-Effects-Interactions pattern. First, update the user's balance, and then transfer the funds.</li></ol><p>Replace the existing <code>CashOut</code> function with this:</p><pre><div class="bg-black rounded-md mb-4"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><span>solidity</span><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"></svg>Copy code</div><div><code class="!whitespace-pre hljs language-solidity">function CashOut(uint _am)
public
payable
{
    if(_am &lt;= balances[msg.sender] &amp;&amp; block.number &gt; lastBlock)
    {
        balances[msg.sender] -= _am;
        (bool success, ) = msg.sender.call{value: _am}("");
        require(success, "Transfer failed.");
        TransferLog.AddMessage(msg.sender, _am, "CashOut");
    }
}
</code></div></div></pre><ol><li>Outdated Solidity version:
