end
</code></div></div></pre><p>In this example, we first define a Julia struct <code>MyMessage</code> to hold the message data. We then create a <code>handle_message</code> function to receive and parse incoming messages. The <code>WebSocket.recv</code> function is used to receive the message string from the websocket, and the <code>ProtoBuf.decode</code> function is used to deserialize the message string into a <code>MyMessage</code> object. We then access the message fields and process the message data as needed.</p><p>To run this code, you'll need to install the <code>WebSockets.jl</code> and <code>ProtoBuf.jl</code> packages. You can do this using the following commands in the Julia REPL:</p><pre><div class="bg-black mb-4 rounded-md"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><span>julia</span><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"></svg>Copy code</div><div><code class="!whitespace-pre hljs language-julia">using Pkg
