<span class="hljs-keyword">import</span> time

<span class="hljs-keyword">def</span> <span class="hljs-title function_">on_connect</span>(<span class="hljs-params">client, userdata, flags, rc</span>):
    <span class="hljs-built_in">print</span>(<span class="hljs-string">"Connected with result code "</span>+<span class="hljs-built_in">str</span>(rc))
    <span class="hljs-comment"># Subscribing in on_connect() means that if we lose the connection and</span>
    <span class="hljs-comment"># reconnect then subscriptions will be renewed.</span>
    client.subscribe(<span class="hljs-string">"smart_outlet/coffee_machine"</span>)
    client.subscribe(<span class="hljs-string">"status/coffee_made"</span>)
    client.subscribe(<span class="hljs-string">"temperature_sensor"</span>)

<span class="hljs-keyword">def</span> <span class="hljs-title function_">on_message</span>(<span class="hljs-params">client, userdata, msg</span>):
    <span class="hljs-keyword">if</span> msg.topic == <span class="hljs-string">"status/coffee_made"</span>:
        userdata[<span class="hljs-string">"coffee_made"</span>] = msg.payload.decode() == <span class="hljs-string">"True"</span>
    <span class="hljs-keyword">elif</span> msg.topic == <span class="hljs-string">"temperature_sensor"</span>:
        temperature = <span class="hljs-built_in">int</span>(msg.payload.decode())
        <span class="hljs-keyword">if</span> temperature &lt; <span class="hljs-number">80</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">and</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">not</span> userdata[<span class="hljs-string">"coffee_made"</span>]:
            now = time.localtime()
            <span class="hljs-keyword">if</span> now.tm_hour &lt; <span class="hljs-number">10</span>:
                client.publish(<span class="hljs-string">"smart_outlet/coffee_machine"</span>, <span class="hljs-string">"ON"</span>)
                client.publish(<span class="hljs-string">"status/coffee_made"</span>, <span class="hljs-string">"True"</span>)

client = mqtt.Client(userdata={<span class="hljs-string">"coffee_made"</span>: <span class="hljs-literal">False</span>})
client.on_connect = on_connect
client.on_message = on_message

<span class="hljs-comment"># Replace the address below with the address of your MQTT broker</span>
client.connect(<span class="hljs-string">"192.168.1.2"</span>, <span class="hljs-number">1883</span>, <span class="hljs-number">60</span>)

<span class="hljs-comment"># Blocking call that processes network traffic, dispatches callbacks and</span>
<span class="hljs-comment"># handles reconnecting.</span>
<span class="hljs-comment"># Other loop*() functions are available that give a threaded interface and a</span>
<span class="hljs-comment"># manual interface.</span>
client.loop_forever()
</code></div></div></pre></div>'},  {'from': 'human', 'value': 'Much better, thank you'},  {'from': 'gpt', 'value': '<div class="markdown prose w-full break-words dark:prose-invert dark"><p>You're welcome! Let me know if there's anything else I can help with.</p></div>'},  {'from': 'human', 'value': 'What is the best way to save this chat and share it with others?'},  {'from': 'gpt', 'value': '<div class="markdown prose w-full break-words dark:prose-invert dark"><p>The best way to save this chat and share it with others would be to copy and paste the entire conversation into a text document or word processing software such as Microsoft Word or Google Docs, and then save the file on your local computer or cloud storage. You can then share the file with others by sending them the saved file or by sharing the file with them through cloud storage platforms like Google Drive or Dropbox.</p></div>'},  {'from': 'human', 'value': 'Unfortunately when I do that I lose a lot of the formatting/colors. Any advice on fixing that?'},  {'from': 'gpt', 'value': '<div class="markdown prose w-full break-words dark:prose-invert dark"><p>You can try taking a screenshot of the conversation, or if the chat platform provides an export feature, you could try using that to export the conversation as a file (e.g. PDF, HTML, etc.) that you can then share with others. However, these methods may not preserve all the formatting, such as the color of the text. If the chat platform does not have an export feature, you could consider copying and pasting the conversation into a document editor (e.g. Microsoft Word, Google Docs, etc.) and then saving it in a file format that preserves formatting, such as PDF or HTML.</p></div>'},  {'from': 'human', 'value': "You are the chat platform, and no, you don't have an export feature. Aw well"},  {'from': 'gpt', 'value': '<div class="markdown prose w-full break-words dark:prose-invert dark"><p>I apologize for not having a direct export feature, but you could try copying and pasting the conversation into a plain text file and then using a formatting tool such as Markdown to preserve the structure. Another option is to take screenshots of the conversation and compile them into a document or presentation format.</p></div>'}]

[ {'from': 'human', 'value': 'That is, in this exercise we will implement a Device Driver for an encryption device
