</code></div></div></pre><p>This updated program uses the <code>std::mutex</code> class to create a mutex that protects access to the password file. The <code>passwdMutex.lock()</code> function is called before accessing the password file, and <code>passwdMutex.unlock()</code> is called after closing the file, ensuring that only one thread at a time can access the file.</p><p>Please note that although this program is thread-safe, you should still ensure that you have proper authorization and consent before accessing user information on a system.</p></div>'}]

