            <span class="hljs-selector-tag">var</span> jwt = new <span class="hljs-built_in">JwtSecurityToken</span>(
                signingCredentials: signingCredentials,
                claims: claims,
                expires: DateTime.UtcNow.AddMinutes(<span class="hljs-number">60</span>)
            );

            <span class="hljs-selector-tag">var</span> token = new <span class="hljs-built_in">JwtSecurityTokenHandler</span>()<span class="hljs-selector-class">.WriteToken</span>(jwt);
            return <span class="hljs-built_in">Ok</span>(new { token });
        }
        return <span class="hljs-built_in">BadRequest</span>();
    }
</code></div></div></pre><ol start="4"><li>Use the [Authorize] attribute to mark controllers or specific actions that require authentication:</li></ol><pre><div class="bg-black mb-4 rounded-md"><div class="flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans"><button class="flex ml-auto gap-2"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-4 w-4" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M16 4h2a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v14a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H6a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V6a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h2"></path><rect x="8" y="2" width="8" height="4" rx="1" ry="1"></rect></svg>Copy code</button></div><div class="p-4 overflow-y-auto"><code class="!whitespace-pre-wrap hljs language-csharp">    [<span class="hljs-meta">Authorize</span>]
    [<span class="hljs-meta">Route(<span class="hljs-string">"api/[controller]"</span>)</span>]
    <span class="hljs-keyword">public</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">class</span> <span class="hljs-title">ValuesController</span> : <span class="hljs-title">Controller</span>
    {
        <span class="hljs-comment">// ...</span>
    }
</code></div></div></pre><ol start="5"><li>Test the API by sending a request with the Authorization header set to "Bearer &lt;JWT&gt;" where JWT is a valid JSON Web Token.</li></ol><p>This example uses the Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.JwtBearer package to handle JWT token validation and the System.IdentityModel.Tokens.Jwt package to create the JWT token.</p><p>It's important to note</p></div>'}]

[ {'from': 'human', 'value': 'I changed the name of my next-auth cookies along with some other config and now by login is broken. 

  cookies: {
    sessionToken: {
      name: "your-custom-session-token-name",
      options: {
